From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:22:18 -0400
Subject: import: imported bookmarks become pinned tabs and folders

After an import that brought bookmarks (the welcome flow or
chrome://settings/importData), the bookmark tree becomes pins in the
window's active Space through the Arc importer's apply path: the bookmark
bar's bookmarks first, then Other bookmarks, every folder a folder, every
bookmark a Space-pinned tab inserted unloaded with the bookmark as its
home, idempotent on the bookmark ids. From then on the bookmark bar never
shows and the star leaves the address row (stedding.bookmarks.converted).
The welcome step says so; a profile that already holds bookmarks converts
them from the bar's "Turn Bookmarks into Pinned Tabs"
(docs/features/import.md I13-I16).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 3, R6-28: PRODUCT has no bookmarks; the
sidebar is the bookmarks.
Removable when: Chromium's vertical tab strip pins bookmarks itself.
